#. type: Title =
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generals, Wizards & Heroes"
msgstr "Généraux, Sorciers & Héros"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:11
msgid ""
"Generals, Wizards and Heroes are represented by a single stand which "
"includes the [.bo5a]#famous individual# plus [.edit]#their# bodyguard, "
"standard bearer, familiars, servants, messengers, observers, courtiers, "
"pets, jesters, toadies and other such hangers-on as make up [.edit]#their# "
"immediate entourage. For the sake of convenience, Generals, Wizards and "
"Heroes are referred to as characters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|image:characters/general.webp[width=534,height=434]\n"
"|image:characters/wizard-1.webp[width=746,height=569]\n"
"\n"
"|General |Wizard\n"
"\n"
"|image:characters/hero.webp[width=514,height=597]\n"
"|image:characters/wizard-2.webp[width=541,height=590]\n"
"\n"
"|Hero | Wizard\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:27
msgid "Generals, Wizards and Heroes are immediately recognisable pieces."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Game values"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block * 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:39
msgid ""
"In some armies, Generals, Wizards and Heroes have different names such as "
"Liche priests in the Undead army and Shamans in the Orc army. Names apart, "
"they amount to the same thing and each is either a General, Wizard or Hero "
"as indicated in the Army Lists section of the rulebook."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block * 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:49
msgid ""
"Unlike troop stands Character stands don’t have a value for Hits or Armour. "
"Instead they have a Command value. They have no Hits value at all. They have "
"an Attack value which is expressed as a bonus, for example +1, +2, +3, etc. "
"The picture below shows an Empire Hero stand with its game values. Full game "
"values for all characters can be found in the Army List section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:60
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|↙ |⤸ |⤹ |↘\n"
"\n"
"<|Attacks +1\n"
"^|[.line-through]## Hits ##\n"
"^|[.line-through]## Armour ##\n"
">|Command 8\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characters as game pieces"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:75
msgid ""
"Characters are different from other pieces in the game.  Most stands of "
"infantry or other warriors represent a substantial body of troops defined by "
"the stand’s area.  Characters represent a comparatively tiny number of "
"actual individuals, some of whom may be scattered across the battlefield in "
"the role of messengers, scouts and observers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:81
msgid ""
"The character stand’s prime function is to provide a fixed point from which "
"orders are issued. In addition a character stand can bolster a unit’s combat "
"ability by joining it. In the case of Wizards they can also cast spells, "
"some of which are directly offensive in nature."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:87
msgid ""
"Because of their unique place in the game, character stands are treated "
"differently to units of troops. A character stand is used much more in the "
"manner of a token or marker. The stand itself is ignored on the battlefield "
"by units from both sides."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:97
msgid ""
"Units from their own side can move through characters without penalty and "
"they, in turn, can move through units from their own side. If friendly units "
"are moved in such a way that they displace a character then the player must "
"immediately move the character by the minimum distance required to allow the "
"unit to take up its position. This may result in a character moving several "
"times during the Command phase to get out of the way of troop movement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:100
msgid ""
"If moved through by enemies, characters are repositioned as <<enemy-moving-"
"through-characters,described below>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:105
msgid ""
"Characters can also be seen through and, where appropriate, shot through by "
"troops from both sides.  Their presence is not considered to block a unit’s "
"line of sight."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:112
msgid ""
"It follows that characters cannot be specifically shot at, targeted with "
"spells or attacked in combat. Characters don’t suffer hits from shooting or "
"combat, although they can be slain if a unit they are with is destroyed, as "
"<<characters-in-combat,described late>>r. A character stand on its own "
"cannot charge or fight an enemy unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:119
msgid ""
"It is worth bearing in mind that character stands are always ignored when "
"considering which enemy target is the closest and when measuring between "
"units. Similarly, an enemy unit cannot act on its initiative with regard to "
"a character and the presence of an enemy character within 20cm does not "
"impose a −1 Command penalty."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:126
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orders from wizards & heroes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:132
msgid ""
"We have already described how characters give orders in the Command phase.  "
"[.bo5a]#This section summarises the principle rules – for details see the "
"rules for xref:command.adoc#orders[Orders].#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:139
msgid ""
"Any character can issue an order to any unit or brigade within his command "
"range. The General’s command range extends over the whole battlefield but a "
"Hero can only issue orders to units within 60cm of the character stand and a "
"Wizard can only issue an order to a unit within 20cm of the character stand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:147
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Character |Command Range\n"
"\n"
"|General   |Battlefield\n"
"|Hero      |60cm\n"
"|Wizard    |20cm\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:154
msgid ""
"A player can issue orders from his characters in any sequence he wishes but "
"must finish issuing orders from each character before moving to the next. "
"For example, you can’t issue orders from the General then from a Hero and "
"then from the General again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:159
msgid ""
"Once a Hero or Wizard has failed to issue an order, that character can issue "
"no more orders in that Command phase. However, other characters can continue "
"issuing orders until they too fail to issue an order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:169
msgid ""
"Once the General has failed to give an order, *no further orders* can be "
"issued in that Command phase by *any* characters even if they have issued no "
"orders previously. This makes it preferable for Heroes and Wizards to issue "
"orders first and the General last, although this is not mandatory. A player "
"may occasionally prefer to await the outcome of his General’s attempts to "
"issue orders before committing a Wizard or Hero."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:174
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blunders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:185
msgid ""
"Wizards and Heroes are not always reliable. We presume that the General has "
"briefed them concerning his battle plan, carefully instructed them in their "
"duties and taken pains to make everything as clear as possible. In a perfect "
"world this should be sufficient but, alas, this is rarely so.  Some "
"underlings are plain dim and so misunderstand their orders. Others get "
"carried away and charge off in pursuit of a new and exciting goal. A few are "
"quick to ignore their General’s orders in favour of their own plan."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:199
msgid ""
"This wayward inclination is taken into account whenever a Wizard or Hero "
"fails to issue an order as a result of rolling a 12. If the player rolls a "
"12 then not only is the order not issued but something has gone wrong. "
"Someone has blundered. The Wizard or Hero has got carried away or ignored "
"the instructions he has been given or taken a wrong turning or mistaken a "
"wandering group of locals for the enemy. The player rolls a dice and "
"consults the <<d6-blunder,Blunder table>>. The result applies to the unit "
"which has failed to receive its order and to all units in the case of a "
"brigade, except where noted otherwise. If it is the first order to the unit/"
"brigade then the half pace move is not allowed. Follow the result of the "
"Blunder table instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:204
msgid ""
"A General doesn’t blunder – [.bo5a]#they are above such things.# However, if "
"the General rolls a 12 the unit/brigade cannot move even if it was its first "
"order and therefore it was eligible for a half pace move."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:207
#, no-wrap
msgid "D6 Blunder"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:209
#, no-wrap
msgid "*1 You must be crazy!*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:219
msgid ""
"The unit’s officers are seriously bewildered by their orders and insist on "
"disputing their interpretation.  This takes a long time during which tempers "
"fray, fists fly and some officers storm off determined to spend the rest of "
"the battle undermining the efforts of their rivals. The unit suffers a −1 "
"Command penalty for the rest of the battle."
msgstr ""

#.  Newline added
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:227
msgid ""
"If a brigade has blundered then this penalty applies to one unit and the "
"player can choose which is affected. The penalty will apply to the whole "
"brigade if an order is given to the brigade that includes the affected unit."
msgstr ""

#.  Newline added
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:234
msgid ""
"This penalty is cumulative so it’s theoretically possible for a unit’s "
"effectiveness to plummet to a seriously incompetent level."
msgstr ""

#.  Newline added
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:239
msgid "The unit/brigade may not move further that Command phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:241
#, no-wrap
msgid "*2–3 Blimey Sir! There’s thousands of ’em!*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:249
msgid ""
"The unit’s officers mistake a shabby group of curious locals for a huge "
"enemy force. If there are no visible enemy units within a full pace move of "
"the unit or brigade then the unit/brigade halts and in this case there is no "
"further penalty."
msgstr ""

#.  Newline added
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:257
msgid ""
"If there are visible enemy units within a full pace move of the blundering "
"unit or brigade then the unit or each unit in a brigade must move "
"[.edit]#by# the shortest route to get [.edit]#beyond# a full pace move from "
"all enemy units."
msgstr ""

#.  Newline added
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:265
msgid ""
"Where units have different moves, the brigade moves at the speed of the "
"slowest. Once it has moved, the unit/brigade halts. If unable to comply, the "
"unit/brigade moves as far away from all enemy units as possible instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:267
#, no-wrap
msgid "*4–5 No sense in getting killed sir!*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:275
msgid ""
"The unit’s officers are timorous and hesitant, convinced that the unit is "
"surrounded by enemy and unseen dangers. The unit/brigade may not move and "
"cannot receive any further orders that Command phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:277
#, no-wrap
msgid "*6 Up and ’at ’em, men!*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:289
msgid ""
"The troops are overcome by a sudden and uncontrollable lust for glory and "
"surge forwards out of control. The unit must move at its maximum full pace "
"towards the nearest visible enemy unit and will charge the nearest enemy "
"unit if it is possible to do so. If a whole brigade goes ‘up and ’at ’em!’ "
"then move each unit one at a time as the movement of one may affect the "
"ability of subsequent units to charge [.edit]#by blocking line of# sight or "
"access to [.edit]#stand# edges."
msgstr ""

#.  Newline added
#. // Remove:
#. //Once
#. //units have moved, they halt as for a normal failed
#. //order.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:302
msgid ""
"Once units have moved, or [.edit]#if# there is no visible enemy, they halt. "
"The unit/brigade cannot receive any further orders that Command phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:308
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/command.adoc:572
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:372
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/siege-and-fortresses.adoc:867
#, no-wrap
msgid "Character movement"
msgstr "Mouvement des personnages"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:312
msgid ""
"We have already covered the essentials of character movement in the Command "
"section. To summarise:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:316
msgid ""
"Characters move at the end of the Command phase and never move in company "
"with units during the Command phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:320
msgid ""
"A character can move once up to 60cm (100cm if flying). No Command test is "
"required for a character to move."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:326
msgid ""
"Characters move in company with units they have joined in other phases. For "
"example, if they are driven back by missile fire, move to make way for other "
"units, and throughout the Combat phase during pursuit, fall backs, retreats "
"and advances"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:329
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characters & terrain"
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling i.e.
#.  "Monstrous and Chariot Mounts" is "Character Mounts".
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:342
msgid ""
"Unless riding monsters or chariots, character stands [.bo5a]#treat# terrain "
"in the same way as infantry [.bo5a]#regardless of whether the actual model "
"is mounted.# Only terrain which is impossible for infantry to cross is "
"impossible for characters (i.e., a character cannot move across the open "
"ocean, into a volcanic lake and so forth). If riding monsters or chariots, "
"characters are restricted by terrain in the same way as these troops. See "
"[.edit]#<<character-mounts>>#."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:347
#, no-wrap
msgid "Joining a unit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:356
msgid ""
"A character may join a unit by moving into touch with it at the end of the "
"Command phase. The player declares that the character is now with the unit. "
"A character can join a unit which is in combat if you wish. Players should "
"be careful not to place characters touching units if they are not intended "
"to be joined and should always leave a discernible gap where this makes the "
"position clear."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:361
msgid ""
"A character must also join a unit if he is obliged to move as a result of "
"enemy troop movement. In this case, he must move into touch with a friendly "
"unit within a 30cm move as <<enemy-moving-through-characters,described "
"below>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:366
msgid ""
"If a character is joined with a unit which is confused, this does not "
"prevent the character from moving at the end of the Command phase. Nor does "
"it prevent him issuing orders to other units during the Command phase itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:384
msgid ""
"The precise position of the character stand relative to a unit he has joined "
"is not critical. Once he has joined a unit, the character himself is assumed "
"to be within the unit’s formation. Once a character has joined a unit, his "
"stand may be moved to any point around the unit as required, for example so "
"that another unit can charge into position or move alongside. The character "
"stand must remain in touch with the unit at some point if possible. If this "
"is impossible, if the unit is in combat and completely surrounded for "
"example, the player can temporarily balance the character stand in the "
"middle of the unit or say that he is doing so whilst placing the stand "
"safely aside. A character joined with a unit that is locked in unresolved "
"combat can still issue orders in the Command phase. Nominate a stand in the "
"unit [.edit]#measure# the distance to the commanded unit from that stand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:387
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enemy moving through characters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:397
msgid ""
"If a lone character gets in the way of enemy units as they move then the "
"character stand must be moved up to 30cm to join a friendly unit. Flying "
"units fly over the battlefield as they move and so only displace characters "
"if their move ends on top of them. Character stands cannot be moved so that "
"they displace enemy characters.  Note that a displaced character does not "
"have to join the closest unit, the player can decide which unit to join."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:402
msgid ""
"If a character cannot move to a friendly unit, he is considered to have been "
"slain and is removed from the battle. If the General is slain, the battle is "
"over as described in the xref:end-of-the-battle.adoc[End of The Battle]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:408
msgid ""
"This is an important rule because it obliges characters to remain fairly "
"close to their own troops, especially Wizards who might otherwise exploit "
"their invulnerability to launch unsupported magical attacks deep behind "
"enemy lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:416
msgid ""
"If a character is with a unit when it makes contact with a moving enemy then "
"the character can be repositioned out of the way as convenient, so long as "
"he stays in touch with the unit he is with. If this is impossible (if the "
"unit is surrounded, for example) then the character can be precariously "
"balanced on top of the unit or removed but assumed to be included within the "
"unit’s formation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:421
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characters & shooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:427
msgid ""
"Characters cannot be shot at but may have joined a unit which is shot at and "
"either been driven back or destroyed as a result. If a character is with a "
"unit that has been driven back by shooting, he automatically moves with it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:431
msgid ""
"If a character has joined a unit that is subsequently destroyed by shooting "
"or which is routed and destroyed as a result of a drive back then the "
"character is slain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:435
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characters that shoot"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:441
msgid ""
"All characters have an Attack bonus expressed as +1, +2 or +3.  If a "
"character can shoot, it has an Attack bonus expressed as +1/1, with the "
"second value being the additional shooting attack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:445
msgid ""
"A character that has a shooting attack can only use it when joined to a unit."
msgstr ""

#. // BO5A addition:
#. If several characters have joined a unit, only one
#. can use its shooting attack.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:460
msgid ""
"Monster mounted characters or other characters that have a shooting attack "
"when joined to units are assumed to be within the unit’s formation "
"regardless of the actual position of the character stand. When shooting in "
"the Shooting phase, or during the Command phase if shooting at chargers, the "
"player chooses one of the unit’s stands and works out the character’s "
"shooting from that stand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:468
msgid ""
"All shots taken at the same enemy unit have to be worked out from the same "
"stand, but otherwise the character can ‘move’ from stand to stand during the "
"turn as required (this can happen during the opposing player’s Command phase "
"if the unit is charged by more than one enemy for example). The same "
"principle applies to characters casting spells."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:471
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characters in combat"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:479
msgid ""
"When one or more characters join a unit in combat, the character with the "
"highest Attack value can add this as a bonus to the Attack value of any one "
"stand in the unit. A unit may be joined by any number of characters but only "
"one character can ever add his Attack value bonus to a unit per round of "
"combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:484
msgid ""
"Character stands which have joined a unit in combat must remain with it "
"whilst the combat lasts and must fall back, stand their ground, retreat, "
"pursue or advance with the unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:489
msgid ""
"A General, Wizard or Hero is slain if the unit he is with is destroyed. This "
"is of particular importance as it makes combat an extremely risky business "
"for characters and certainly not something to be indulged in lightly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:492
#, no-wrap
msgid "Character mounts"
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling modelled
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:505
msgid ""
"If you read the Army Lists section you’ll see that Generals, Wizards and "
"Heroes are often allowed to ride on some sort of monster or in a chariot. In "
"the case of monsters these are referred to as *Monstrous Mounts* and "
"chariots are *Chariot Mounts*. Sometimes characters are allowed to ride on "
"some *Special Mounts* that have their own special description in appropriate "
"army lists. In all other cases where characters are modelled riding on "
"common mounts (or simply *mounts*) like horses, wolves and similar "
"creatures, they do so for free."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:516
msgid ""
"If a character rides either a Monstrous or Chariot Mount this does not "
"affect the rules described above. The stand is still a General, Wizard or "
"Hero stand for our purposes.  However, the mount will usually increase the "
"character’s Attack value bonus in combat. Chariot and Monster Mount bonuses "
"are added to the character’s normal Combat bonus. In addition, there may be "
"special rules that apply. For example, a General riding a Monstrous Mount "
"may cause terror. These rules are noted in the Army Lists."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:520
msgid ""
"It is quite common for characters to ride some sort of flying creature such "
"as a Griffon or a Dragon. This increases the rider’s maximum movement to "
"100cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:524
msgid ""
"A flying character is not affected by normally impassable terrain because it "
"can fly right over it in the same way as other flying stands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:536
msgid ""
"A character riding a chariot or a monster cannot move into terrain that his "
"mount could not enter. He cannot enter a wood for example. He cannot join a "
"unit if all of its stands are in a wood. If a unit he is with retreats, "
"falls back, pursues, is driven back, advances or is otherwise obliged to "
"move into a wood he must move up to 30cm to another unit in the same way as "
"a lone character contacted by the enemy. If he cannot do so, he is slain. "
"However, so long as at least one stand in a unit is positioned in "
"unrestricted terrain, the character can join the unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:541
msgid ""
"Note that common mounts such as horses, wolves, boars and similar creatures "
"are not accorded any special rules, and characters riding these are simply "
"treated the same way as characters on foot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:544
#, no-wrap
msgid "Odd size character bases"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:552
msgid ""
"Characters are mounted on standard sized bases in the same way as troop "
"stands – however many players prefer to mount their characters on round "
"bases as this makes them easier to spot. In addition, some of the special "
"character models, such as the Grand Theogonist, are too large to fit onto "
"the standard sized base."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:558
msgid ""
"Character stands can be mounted onto round bases up to 25mm in diameter "
"using the normal rules. Simply measure distances to the stand’s edge as you "
"would for a rectangular base. This confers no significant advantage over a "
"standard base."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/characters.adoc:568
msgid ""
"Character stands can be mounted onto larger bases, whether rectangular, "
"round or whatever, but in these cases all distances must be measured either "
"to the centre of the base or to a specific point on the base such as a "
"particular model. Players must point out where they will measure from before "
"the game. Oversized bases are slightly inconvenient in play, but allow for "
"some very nice decorative models or more complex scenes and do look very "
"attractive."
msgstr ""
